# AGMX — Cloudflare Pages rewrites (port of vercel.json rewrites)
# Pages applies the first matching rule; static redirects go before splats.
# /config.js is served by functions/config.js.js; /api/health by
# functions/api/health.js (Functions take precedence over these rules).
# No route rules: a top-level 404.html was uploaded so Pages' built-in SPA
# fallback is off, and Pages already serves app.html at /app (clean URLs).
# Declaring /app -> /app.html 200 here collided with that canonicalization
# and produced a 308 redirect loop.
# /auth/callback is the Supabase redirect target for Google sign-in and
# password reset; it has no clean-URL sibling, so this rewrite cannot collide.
/auth/callback /callback.html 200

